M1: Circuit/Boolean/{HardCore,XorLemma}, nonuniform De Morgan circuits, size = complexity interpretation (single g).
- IsHardCoreMeasure f s δ ε M: M∈[0,1], δ2^n ≤ ΣM, complexity g ≤ s ⇒ Σ_{g=f} M ≤ (1/2+ε)ΣM.
- exists_isHardCoreMeasure (Impagliazzo): 0<δ, 0<ε, 1 ≤ 3ε²δ²T, (complexity g ≤ T*s+(2+T*(2*(T+2))) ⇒ #{g=f}/2^n ≤ 1-δ) ⇒ ∃ M, IsHardCoreMeasure f s δ ε M; _of_le: size S gives (S-(2+T(2(T+2))))/T.
- card_eq_sum_le: XOR lemma for a measure, any Fintype.
- IsHardCoreMeasure.card_eq_xorPower_div_le; card_eq_xorPower_div_le (Yao, hardness at T(s+3)+2+2T(T+2)): complexity g ≤ s ⇒ #{g=xorPower f k}/2^(kn) ≤ 1/2+ε+(1/2-ε)(1-δ)^k.
Proof: boosting with Boosting.weight/potential, rate εδ; strict majority; XOR by 1=M+(1-M) induction.
Checks: run-gates all six ok; tests ComplexityTests/HardnessAmplification incl. parity-2 hard-core instance, 4 axiom guards.
Credit: Impagliazzo95, Yao82, Holenstein05. Contributors: worker-sable-loop.
Limits: measure not set; nonuniform. Continuation M2: worst→average, NW/IW/BFNW endpoints.
